			<div class="content" id="post-content-673531">
									

<p>As a somewhat trifling style tip-</p>
<p>I've been seeing a number of recent SCPs opening their description with "appears to be" or "seems to be". In some cases this is appropriate, such as when there is reason to doubt the SCP's actual physical form, or when the SCP's effects/abnormalities are perception-related.</p>
<p>However, if it's a dog, JUST SAY IT'S A DOG. Even if it's a ~spooky~ dog. And especially if you're going to use the word "apparently" immediately after, in the same sentence.</p>

